solution.text:
Molarity $=\frac{\text { mass } \times 1000}{\text { molecular weight } \times \text { volume of solution }}$
Molecular weight of ethyl alcohol,
$$
\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{C}_{2} \mathrm{H}_{5} \mathrm{OH} &=12 \times 2+5+16+1 \\
&=24+22=46 \mathrm{g} \mathrm{mol}^{-1}
\end{aligned}
$$
On substituting the values, we get
$$
\begin{array}{l}
0.5 \mathrm{M}=\frac{\text { mass } \times 1000}{46 \times 100} \\
\text { Mass }=\frac{0.5 \times 46}{10}=2.3 \mathrm{g}
\end{array}
$$
$\therefore$ Volume of ethyl alcohol required.
$$
V=\frac{\text { mass of ethyl alcohol }}{\text { density of ethyl alcohol }}=\frac{2.3 \mathrm{g}}{1.15 \mathrm{g} / \mathrm{cc}}=2 \mathrm{cc}
$$
